      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The numerator's degree is not less than the denominator's, so divide first: \\( \\frac{x^{2}}{x^{2} - 4} = 1 + \\frac{4}{x^{2} - 4} \\), and write \\( \\frac{4}{x^{2} - 4} = \\frac{A}{x - 2} + \\frac{B}{x + 2} \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Clearing denominators gives \\( 4 = A \\left(x + 2\\right) + B \\left(x - 2\\right) \\). Setting \\( x = 2 \\) gives \\( A = 1 \\), and setting \\( x = -2 \\) gives \\( B = -1 \\), so the integrand is \\( 1 - \\frac{1}{x + 2} + \\frac{1}{x - 2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
